facts:
Two angles forming a **right angle** add to $90^{\circ}$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\draw (0,0)--(40:2.2);
\draw (0.32,0)--(0.32,0.32)--(0,0.32);
\node at (1.17,0.43) {$a$};
\node at (0.53,1.13) {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Angles on a **straight line** add to $180^{\circ}$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (-2.5,0)--(2.5,0);
\draw (0,0)--(65:2.1);
\node at (-0.67,1.05) {$a$};
\node at (1.05,0.67) {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Angles **at a point** (around a vertex) add to $360^{\circ}$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0)--(0:2.1);
\draw (0,0)--(110:2.1);
\draw (0,0)--(225:2.1);
\node at (0.72,1.02) {$a$};
\node at (-1.22,0.27) {$b$};
\node at (0.48,-1.15) {$c$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

